      <VerificationBadge verifiedDate="27 October 2026" topic="PDC World Darts Championship 2026/27 Confirmed Qualifiers & Route Allocations" />

      <!-- Section 1: Overview -->
      <section class="content-card">
        <h2>128-Player Field Architecture &amp; Selection Criteria</h2>
        <p>
          The expanded 128-player World Darts Championship field is populated through three distinct qualification pillars established by the Professional Darts Corporation (PDC) and the Professional Dart Players Association (PDPA):
        </p>
        <ol>
          <li>
            <strong>PDC Order of Merit (Top 40):</strong> The top 40 players from the two-year rolling world rankings. The top 32 receive protected seeded positions in the draw.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>PDC ProTour Order of Merit (Next 40):</strong> The top 40 non-qualified players based on floor performance across the single-season Players Championship and European Tour events.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>International &amp; Secondary Pathways (48 Places):</strong> A global network of 48 berths comprising secondary developmental tours, women's professional pathways, regional continental affiliate circuits, and final Tour Card holder knockouts.
          </li>
        </ol>
        <p>
          While the top 40 Order of Merit and ProTour places remain fluid until the ranking cut-off at the <strong>Players Championship Finals in Minehead (27–29 November 2026)</strong>, international affiliate tournaments and secondary tours conclude throughout autumn. For detailed mathematical rules on how seeds and roll-downs operate, read our complete <a href="/tournament/qualification-explained/">World Championship Qualification Guide</a> and check real-time rankings on our <a href="/tournament/order-of-merit/">PDC Order of Merit Guide</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 2: Complete 48-Slot Table -->
      <section class="content-card">
